    main_idea: "The self-made individual narrative obscures the collective preconditions of individual success and produces ideological consequences that systematically misattribute structural outcomes to personal virtue or failure.",
    tone: "critical, sociologically informed",
    key_inference: "The political argument that wealth taxation is confiscatory depends partly on the self-made myth; if success reflects collective investment, taxation is more plausibly understood as a return on that investment.",
